WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.230
It was just a small wish.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.730
I only wanted to smile with her...

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.110
and gently embrace her.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.620
But what came to greet us instead
was a time of conflict,

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.370
stolen powers, broken staves,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.210
new and mysterious
opponents we must battle,

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.460
and a loss of direction.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.470
But despite all of that, we will...

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:40.010
Mahou Shoujo Lyrical
Nanoha A's will now begin.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.370
According to the scans,
her injuries aren't too serious.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:13.170
The source of her magic, her Linker Core,
has simply shrunk to a very unusual size.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.590
I see. So it really is connected
to the other recent cases.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.220
Yes. There's no doubt about it now.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.390
I wonder if we'll have to
push back our break now...

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.930
At this rate, some of these recent
cases will probably be assigned to us.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.470
That's just how it goes in this line of work.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.700
Reunion and Moving!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.790
It's good to hear that you
weren't badly injured, either.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.510
Chrono, sorry for worrying you like this.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.430
It's fine, I'm already used
to it from you and Nanoha.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.270
You're young, so it's no surprise that
your Linker Core is already recovering.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.900
However, you won't be able to use
magic for a bit, so be careful, okay?

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.030
Yes! Thank you very much!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.200
Ah, Enforcer Harlaown.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.540
Do you have a minute?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.160
Yes. What is it?

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.000
Walk with me.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:35.960
Is something wrong...?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.000
Actually, regarding <i>that</i> matter...

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.550
Fate-chan...

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.260
Nanoha...

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:58.560
U-Um... I'm sorry our reunion
turned out like this...

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.690
Are you okay?

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:03.740
Yeah... it's just a scratch.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.280
Never mind that, are you...

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.910
I'm fine, too. It's all thanks to you
and everyone else, Fate-chan.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.660
I'm full of energy!

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.790
Fate-chan?

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.250
Fate-chan...

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.750
Nanoha!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.340
Sorry... it looks like
I'm still a little dizzy.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.720
Yeah...

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.220
Thanks for saving me, Fate-chan.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.480
And... I'm really happy that
we're able to meet again.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.070
Yeah, me too.
I'm so happy to see you again.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.180
Nanoha! Fate!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.680
Yuuno-kun! Arf-san!

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.140
Nanoha, it's been so long!

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:16.930
Nanoha.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.860
Everyone...

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.240
Bardiche...

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.910
I'm sorry... because I wasn't
strong enough, you...

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.660
How extensive is the damage?

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.680
To be honest,
it doesn't look too good...

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.600
Their automatic repair systems are working,

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.850
but once structural repairs are complete,

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:49.510
they'll need to be reactivated, and a
lot of parts will need to be replaced.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.130
I see...

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:58.890
Now that we're on the subject,
wasn't their magic kind of weird?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.200
It was more than likely Belkan.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.310
Belkan?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:07.150
It's a form of magic that split off from
Midchildan magic a long time ago.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.620
A magic which focuses on
close-quarters combat,

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.250
as opposed to long-distance
and wide-area attacks.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:16.040
Those skilled in it call
themselves knights.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.910
If I remember correctly... that woman
called herself a Belkan knight...

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:25.540
They're most notable for the
"Cartridge System" used in their devices.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.550
By loading cartridges containing
large amounts of compressed magic,

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:33.590
their devices temporarily gain
explosive and destructive power.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.850
It's incredibly dangerous.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:39.930
I see...

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.690
Thanks for trying your
hardest, Raising Heart.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.440
Take this time to rest up.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.750
Fate, it's about time for the interview.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:56.630
Yeah...

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.620
Nanoha, could you come with us?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.380
Yuuno-kun, Arf.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.550
Amy.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:12.300
I just finished ordering the parts
needed for Raising Heart and Bardiche.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:17.220
They said they would have them ready
by the end of today or tomorrow.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:18.640
Thank you very much!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:24.450
And also... we were officially put
in charge of this situation.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.150
What? But what about the
Arthra's maintenance?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.150
Yeah, there's that, too...

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.150
Oh yeah, do either of you
know where Chrono-kun is?

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.330
He said something about some
interview with him, Nanoha, and Fate.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:37.660
It sounded like it was with some important
person in the Administrative Bureau, but...

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.540
We're here.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.840
Chrono. It's been a while.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.920
It has indeed.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.720
They call me a probation officer,
but it's only in name.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:03.730
I heard all about you and your involvement
in the previous incident from Admiral Lindy.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.560
She told me you're a very kind girl.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.230
Thank you very much.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.610
Admiral Graham was Chrono's mentor.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.610
He's a real veteran.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:18.210
In his prime, he was the
commander of an entire fleet,

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.950
and later, he became the Chief Enforcer.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.420
He's such an important person!

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.330
Yeah, but he's a really nice guy.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.790
He's kind to everyone.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.850
Nanoha-kun, I hear that you're Japanese?

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:35.470
Hearing that really brings back
memories of Japan's landscape.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:40.550
I come from the same world as you.
I'm an Englishman.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.440
Really?!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.060
Most of the people from our world
don't have any magical power.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.440
But once in a while,

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:52.070
people like you and me, who have
great magical potential, appear.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:58.160
It's funny. You encountered
magic the same way I did.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.870
Though in my case, I saved a clerk
from the Administrative Bureau.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.710
Though that story's
over fifty years old now.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.310
Fate-kun, you're...
Nanoha-kun's friend, correct?

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:24.970
Yes.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.030
I only want you to
promise me one thing.

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:33.940
Never betray your friends
or those who believe in you.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:39.950
If you can do that much,
I'll promise not to restrict your actions.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.620
Can you do that?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.080
Yes. Absolutely.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.580
Good answer.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.260
Admiral, it's possible that
you've already heard...

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:01.090
but I'm leading the recon team in search
of the Book of Darkness Lost Logia.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.680
I see, so you are.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.350
I probably don't need to say this,
but don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.480
I'll be fine.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.560
After all, calmness is your greatest friend in an emergency,

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.530
just as you taught me, Admiral.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.870
Ah, I did, didn't I?

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:18.820
Well, then...

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.000
Hayate-chan, I've finished
preparing the bath.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.790
Okay. Thanks.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:38.260
Vita-chan, come in with us.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.010
Okay.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.690
You have to be at the hospital
first thing tomorrow morning.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.720
You shouldn't stay up too late tonight.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.100
Okay.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.320
Well, then...

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.480
Signum, what'll you do about your bath?

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.480
I'll be fine for tonight.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.490
I'll bathe tomorrow morning.

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:56.370
Is that so?

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.480
That's surprising coming
from the bath-lover.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.040
I just have these days occasionally.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.000
Well then, we'll be heading in.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:03.950
Alright.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.370
Is it because of today's battle?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.670
You're sharp.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.080
It's as you said.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.800
She cut through your armor, huh...?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.430
Her swordsmanship was excellent.

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.800
She must've learned from a great teacher.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.810
If our weapons were evenly matched,
it could have been a difficult fight.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.310
But...

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.810
even then, you probably still wouldn't lose.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.310
Indeed...

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.320
Thanks, Shamal.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.290
That feels good.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.950
That's what's most important.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.830
It really is like paradise in here.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:57.040
For our knight's pride as Wolkenritter...

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.910
Oh my, Fate-san.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.190
Admiral Lindy.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:29.200
What? Lindy-san is going
to adopt Fate-chan?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:35.000
Yep. Nothing's been finalized yet,
but there's definitely been talk of adoption.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:39.000
After the Presea incident,
Fate-chan was very lonely,

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.640
so the captain asked her
to become her daughter.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:46.010
Fate-chan's still going through
a lot with Presea and everything.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:50.230
We're waiting until she can sort
out her feelings on the matter.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.020
I see...

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.770
What do you think
about it, Nanoha-chan?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:59.860
Umm... I think that'd be really nice.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:01.860
I see.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:08.000
But if that happens, that would
make Chrono-kun onii-chan, huh?

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.040
To Fate-chan, that is.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.410
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:15.700
But those two get along pretty well, so
they might actually be really good siblings.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.090
Chrono.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:23.960
Captain.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.470
Ah, Fate, you're here, too?

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.840
Yeah.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.840
Have you looked over our next mission?

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.180
Yes. I read through it earlier.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:39.400
Nanoha's world is at the center of the
Serial Mage Assaults Incident, right?

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:45.290
Yes. It's limited to an area within personal
teleportation distance from Nanoha's world.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:49.460
Though that area of space is
pretty far from the main office.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.200
Without using a relay port, we won't
be able to teleport ourselves there.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:55.880
It must be painful, not being
able to use the Arthra...

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.710
It would be nice if there was
an open ship we could use.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:03.210
They said that no long-range cruisers
will be available for the next two months.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.550
I see...

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.970
That aside, are you
all right with this, Fate?

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:09.380
With what?

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:13.690
You're a temporary worker, but when it comes
down to it, you're an external collaborator.

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:16.270
I'm not going to force you to
involve yourself in this mission.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:21.650
I can't bring myself to sit around when
both you and Admiral Lindy are in trouble.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.830
Arf said she'd join in too,
so please let us help.

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:29.150
I see. I'm grateful, but...

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.160
I knew it, we should go with <i>that!</i>

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:36.580
"That"?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:44.680
Now then, as the Arthra's crew, we have
been assigned to recover another Lost Logia,

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:50.340
the Book of Darkness, as well as to
investigate the Serial Mage Assault Incident.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:54.440
However, because the Arthra will
be out of commission for a while,

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:58.850
we will set up a temporary base in the
area where the events first began.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.230
We will break up into the following teams.
Our observation staff, Alex and Randy.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.190
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:06.570
Garret will lead Investigation Team 1.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.570
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:14.450
In command will be myself, Enforcer Chrono,
Enforcer Adjutant Amy, and Fate-san.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.450
All of you are to be stationed
together with your respective teams.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:21.840
Finally, the command team will be living in a
neighborhood close to Nanoha-san's house.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:25.420
For Nanoha-san's protection, of course!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.930
This is amazing!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.440
This neighborhood is awesome!

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:39.230
You're right!

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.060
Yeah!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:40.680
See?

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.430
My house is right over there!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.780
Yuuno-kun, Arf...
that's the form you take here?

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.710
My new look, puppy form!

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:01.790
If we're not in these forms in front
of Nanoha and Fate's friends...

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.290
It sounds like you guys will
be going through a lot, too.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.760
Arf, you're so small!
What happened?

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:11.260
Yuuno-kun, it's been so long since
you were in ferret mode!

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.230
Aren't I the cutest?

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:14.260
Yeah!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.270
Nanoha, Fate, your friends are here.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:22.360
Okay!

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.150
Good afternoon.

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:25.270
We're here!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.650
Arisa-chan, Suzuka-chan!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:30.580
Nice to meet you. Or well, I
guess that sounds a little weird.

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:33.200
We've already met a bunch of times
through the video letters, huh?

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:33.900
Yeah.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.910
But I'm so glad to meet you two
in person, Arisa, Suzuka.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:38.460
Yeah!

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:39.370
Me too.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.800
Fate-san, are these your friends?

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:43.870
Hello!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.870
Hello. You two must be
Suzuka-san and Arisa-san, right?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:48.760
Yes...

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.050
How did you know...

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.350
I saw the video letters.

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:53.880
Oh, I see!

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.380
If you'd like, please come in for a cup of tea.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.480
Let's go to my family's cafe, then!

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:59.480
Good idea.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:03.890
This would be a good time to
go meet with your parents.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.390
Just wait a sec, okay?

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.240
She sure is pretty.

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:10.030
Is she your mom, Fate?

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.400
Umm... that's...

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.400
Right now... not exactly...

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.990
Yuuno-kun, it's been so long!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:30.090
I feel like I've seen you somewhere before...

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:31.630
Maybe it's just my imagination.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:44.850
So I'll be living in your
neighborhood for the time being.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.360
Please take good care of me.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.820
Ah, no, no.
I should be the one saying that.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:50.350
Please come by often.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.580
Fate-chan's in third grade, right?

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:54.860
Which school will she be going to?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.070
Well, actually...

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.620
Admira— er, Lindy-san...

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.120
Yes? What is it?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.120
Umm... this...

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.460
could this be...

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.710
I took care of the transfer paperwork.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.210
You'll be Nanoha-san's
classmate starting Monday.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.800
Oh? How wonderful!

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:15.850
Seishou Elementary School it is, huh?

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:18.350
It's a great school.
Right, Nanoha?

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:18.970
Yeah!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.810
That's wonderful, Fate-chan.

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:27.470
Umm... uh... yes,
thank you... very much.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:33.620
The Book of Darkness Lost Logia's
most troublesome part

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.360
is how its energy source works.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:41.360
The Book of Darkness steals a mage's
magical power by devouring their Linker Core.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.580
So Nanoha-chan's Linker Core
was one of the victims?

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.580
Yeah... there's no doubt about it.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.420
When the Book of Darkness
devours someone's Linker Core...

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:53.180
it fills pages depending on
how much magical power it collected.

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:57.800
And the Book of Darkness is
complete once every page is filled.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.840
What will happen once it's complete?

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:04.890
Nothing good, at least...

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.090
You're finally here.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:36.090
Yeah.

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.340
The Administrative Bureau will
probably start moving faster...

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.970
We'll have to change tactics.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.190
It looks like we'll have to operate
away from here for a while.

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:47.770
We should collect as much as we can in the worlds away from here.

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:50.430
How many pages are we up to now?

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.900
340 pages.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:59.410
Thanks to that girl in white the other day,
we've collected quite a bit.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:02.410
Alright!
We've passed the halfway mark!

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:05.280
Let's gather the last bit
and finish it already!

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:10.130
If we hurry and complete it,
we'll be able to live in peace forever...

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:11.790
Together with Hayate...

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:20.090
Shall we go, then?
We don't have much time.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.090
Yes.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.800
Let's go, Laevatein!

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:25.300
To victory.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.350
Guide me, Klarwind!

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:29.050
Activating.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.770
Let's do this, Graf Eisen!

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:32.850
Let's go!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.720
Now then, let us part ways
and meet here at daybreak.

00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:02.170
Vita, don't get too carried away.

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:04.420
I know!

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:17.240
Yes? This is Amy.

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:21.560
Ah, Amy-senpai. I'm Mari, from
the main office's maintenance staff.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.820
Ah, what is it?
What happened?

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:28.540
It's about the two Intelligent Devices you left with us...

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.950
They're acting kind of strange.

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:35.050
We finished repairing and
replacing the parts, but...

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:37.170
their error messages still won't go away.

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:38.050
Error messages?

00:22:38.050 --> 00:22:38.870
What kind?

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:42.430
Well... they're still saying they
don't have the necessary parts.

00:22:42.430 --> 00:22:44.130
I'll send you a summary
of the data report.

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:47.630
Ah, it just got here.

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:51.140
Huh? These are the parts
they still don't have?

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:54.930
Yes... this has to be a mistake, right?

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:08.040
Neither device is accepting commands,
and they keep reporting that message.

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:10.200
It's become a bit of a problem, and...

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:13.700
<i>Raising Heart... Bardiche...
are you both serious?</i>

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:18.120
<i>CVK-792...</i>

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:22.960
<i>That's the Belkan Cartridge System...</i>

00:25:09.820 --> 00:25:13.370
Fate-chan joining our class,
and a new battle!

00:25:13.370 --> 00:25:15.570
I'm fully prepared for both of them.

00:25:15.570 --> 00:25:20.450
Raising Heart and Bardiche have
also returned to us all fixed up, but...

00:25:20.450 --> 00:25:22.790
What?!
Could this be...?!

00:25:22.790 --> 00:25:25.680
Next time on
Mahou Shoujo Lyrical Nanoha A's:

00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:26.790
Episode Four:

00:25:26.790 --> 00:25:28.790
New Powers, Activate!

00:25:29.380 --> 00:25:30.260
All together now...

00:25:30.260 --> 00:25:32.670
Drive Ignition!
